{"h":3106,"lines":[{"w":0.018796992301940915,"h":0.015988371407532731,"c":1,"t":"F","x":0.071428571443014496,"y":0.64389534902007084},{"x":0.81165626557846793,"t":"Reading","y":0.087552383722180216,"w":0.078100770314534551,"c":1,"h":0.01747380174979507},{"w":0.68121342976888022,"h":0.02974113862282679,"t":"Another discovery is that oxytocin's effects vary depending on who we are","c":1,"x":0.11993470600555042,"y":0.1241118271906867},{"x":0.12751843497837134,"t":"interacting with. Studies conducted by Carolyn DeClerck of the University of","h":0.026408433146578036,"c":1,"y":0.14576670441914252,"w":0.69046066284179686},{"y":0.16401795106487316,"w":0.69803939819335936,"h":0.028667012722509044,"c":1,"t":"Antwerp, Belgium, revealed that people who had received a dose of oxytocin","x":0.12747645541801775},{"w":0.65864578247070316,"c":1,"h":0.026505235081247136,"y":0.18293635111706252,"x":0.12748084037193952,"t":"actually became less cooperative when dealing with complete strangers."},{"t":"Meanwhile, Carsten De Dreu at the University of Amsterdam in the Netherlands","w":0.72068308512369794,"h":0.029793367797301351,"x":0.12928816110808253,"y":0.20073820845866197,"c":1},{"w":0.74697291056315118,"c":1,"h":0.028238921647523285,"t":"discovered that volunteers given oxytocin showed favouritism: Dutch men became","x":0.12746442177434336,"y":0.21945515106499958},{"x":0.1256629258743637,"h":0.031625305539319748,"t":"quicker to associate positive words with Dutch names than with foreign ones,","w":0.70010294596354172,"y":0.23599515441140773,"c":1},{"y":0.25711733188645736,"x":0.12379394137334904,"h":0.026463331135334056,"c":1,"t":"for example. According to De Dreu, oxytocin drives people to care for those in","w":0.7073272196451823},{"t":"their social circles and defend them from outside dangers. So, it appears that","y":0.27450324472741539,"x":0.12549968552665217,"w":0.70193868001302084,"h":0.030409592470659108,"c":1},{"x":0.12548157003730911,"c":1,"y":0.29236761661227495,"h":0.03307709383795665,"w":0.69071609497070319,"t":"oxytocin strengthens biases, rather than promoting general goodwill, as was"},{"t":"previously thought.","x":0.12563288855814936,"y":0.31337306111328922,"h":0.019935516411461407,"c":1,"w":0.17358018239339196},{"h":0.03033091587476866,"c":1,"t":"There were signs of these subtleties from the start. Bartz has recently shown that","y":0.34820977387475738,"x":0.12181657329226103,"w":0.73949223836263023},{"w":0.70375803629557288,"h":0.028846667032432216,"t":"in almost half of the existing research results, oxytocin influenced only certain","y":0.36829142082320021,"c":1,"x":0.12177452327505288},{"y":0.38602105601612391,"c":1,"w":0.71700495402018227,"h":0.030425575880258293,"x":0.1217157215650309,"t":"individuals or in certain circumstances. Where once researchers took no notice"},{"y":0.40521515648990958,"x":0.12183214741848995,"w":0.68680852254231772,"h":0.028824340122711734,"c":1,"t":"of such findings, now a more nuanced understanding of oxytocin's effects is"},{"t":"propelling investigations down new lines. To Bartz, the key to understanding what","h":0.02948064122442573,"c":1,"x":0.12186674908620877,"y":0.42427277193506963,"w":0.73938440958658846},{"w":0.74325602213541664,"y":0.441524825335043,"x":0.11992038081030462,"c":1,"t":"the hormone does lies in pinpointing its core function rather than in cataloguing its","h":0.030691943933176091},{"t":"seemingly endless effects. There are several hypotheses which are not mutually","x":0.1199776715139393,"y":0.46200562069979445,"w":0.72819712320963537,"h":0.028274905812103235,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.11996832050387288,"y":0.47982957952323269,"w":0.68683039347330732,"t":"exclusive. Oxytocin could help to reduce anxiety and fear. Or it could simply","h":0.028969771464409932},{"t":"motivate people to seek out social connections. She believes that oxytocin acts as","h":0.028338202030061543,"y":0.4994219831497767,"c":1,"x":0.11811717782464588,"w":0.74689254760742196},{"w":0.73942982991536466,"y":0.51759270638753263,"t":"a chemical spotlight that shines on social clues - a shift in posture, a flicker of the","x":0.11805428671993903,"h":0.029729210631891823,"c":1},{"w":0.74121607462565109,"c":1,"y":0.5367264685860752,"x":0.11814324242214742,"h":0.02676078663744319,"t":"eyes, a dip in the voice - making people more attuned to their social environment."},{"x":0.11804972982673291,"t":"This would explain why it makes us more likely to look others in the eye and","w":0.68863001505533861,"y":0.55503928027562677,"c":1,"h":0.027232966573485617},{"y":0.57210190279934703,"h":0.030063793725224386,"t":"improves our ability to identify emotions. But it could also make things worse for","x":0.1160584082352627,"w":0.72633483886718753,"c":1},{"y":0.59218289420667913,"h":0.028252070439836796,"c":1,"t":"people who are overly sensitive or prone to interpreting social cues in the","w":0.66422358194986975,"x":0.11624757973027044},{"x":0.11645805248607985,"c":1,"y":0.61163042521660538,"w":0.099790662129720042,"t":"worst light.","h":0.018018218984315215},{"w":0.70372187296549482,"h":0.028889172781841665,"y":0.64693687274029554,"x":0.11430330877830329,"t":"Perhaps we should not be surprised that the oxytocin story has become more","c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.030155627710621191,"y":0.66582126742218262,"t":"perplexing. The hormone is found in everything from octopuses to sheep, and its","x":0.11431845656835321,"w":0.7300521341959636},{"w":0.73185974121093755,"c":1,"y":0.68465288173048389,"h":0.029065700169923714,"t":"evolutionary roots stretch back half a billion years. 'It's a very simple and ancient","x":0.11431299522870234},{"c":1,"h":0.027803874215385771,"t":"molecule that has been co-opted for many different functions,' says Sue Carter at","x":0.11435752456581952,"w":0.73745142618815107,"y":0.70409626564581451},{"x":0.11237581629094374,"w":0.72256484985351566,"h":0.028264966229047617,"y":0.72174267490096722,"t":"the University of Illinois, Chicago, USA. 'It affects primitive parts of the brain like","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.11238749195093854,"t":"the amygdala, so it's going to have many effects on just about everything.' Bartz","w":0.72631744384765629,"y":0.73938400045423425,"h":0.029901296955803791},{"c":1,"t":"agrees. 'Oxytocin probably does some very basic things, but once you add our","x":0.11054266114173771,"h":0.032251543485957157,"y":0.75716547196833417,"w":0.71688242594401042},{"h":0.028732051714266515,"y":0.77835627807108176,"c":1,"x":0.11052642607460986,"t":"higher-order thinking and social situations, these basic processes could manifest","w":0.73380874633789062},{"x":0.10867968178934238,"w":0.60205602010091142,"y":0.79639666611580395,"h":0.025629723985503783,"c":1,"t":"in different ways depending on individual differences and context.'"}],"w":2400}